    "C": "Common variable immunodeficiency can cause recurrent infections, but the gastrointestinal symptoms and overall picture are more suggestive of cystic fibrosis.",
    "D": "Cystic fibrosis classically causes recurrent chest infections, failure to thrive, and malabsorption with diarrhoea."
